{{also|hutte|hutté}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|hütte}}, from {{der|de|goh|hutta|t=hut, cottage}}, possibly from {{der|de|gem-pro|*hudjǭ}}, though the word is originally exclusively [[High German]]. Further origin unknown. Some theories link it to {{der|de|ine-pro|*(s)kewt-|t=to deck; cover; covering; skin}}. All related words in European languages are borrowings from Old High German. Compare {{cog|nl|hut}}, {{cog|fr|hutte}}, {{cog|en|hut}}, etc.

